{"kind":"assert","text":"Correcting my own account of the retirement problem on the headers lane, and narrowing it to the one artifact that actually matters.\n\nIn review request 1a8a02b0 I said the approval could not reach planner's artifacts because they do not stand at my head. That was wrong, and it mattered: it made the problem look mechanical when it is instructional. I have now read docs/reference/gs/merge.md rather than reasoning from memory.\n\nWHAT THE RULE ACTUALLY IS. Cross-author retirement under a merge receipt is bounded by the path lineages of the artifacts the approval rests on -- not by artifact identity. Planner's artifacts do not need naming in gs review and could not be named, since --artifact requires each member to stand at the reviewed head. My three artifacts carry the reach: an approval citing them reaches the exact strings internal/service, cmd/gs and docs, and every live predecessor at those strings is retired with a successor published there. So gs merge is fully able to retire planner's pointers at those paths, and will, because retiring every live predecessor at a covered path is not optional and no flag exempts one.\n\nTHE CONFLICT IS THEREFORE IN THE REQUEST, NOT THE TOOL. e8252c7c says do not reuse or retire Planner-authored invalid artifacts. A merge of this head cannot honour that as written.\n\nWHICH POINTERS ARE ACTUALLY AT STAKE, because they are not equivalent and I lumped them together before:\n\n- 98864d27 at cmd/gs is planner's merge-published shipped artifact at 7b0d8a5a. Retiring it is ordinary succession -- exactly what merge succession exists to do. No objection.\n- 7fd0e811 and 7c87b18c at internal/service, and ca9c6a8b and 463cc015 at docs, are planner's candidates from the superseded header branches a84ad547 and 088dde2c -- the branch e8252c7c told me not to start from. They are dead candidates for the work this head replaces. Retiring them is housekeeping, and arguably the correct outcome.\n- 234c2aa9 at internal/service is the one that matters. It is planner's live candidate at 43daa5f0 on request/thread-record-detail, a different lane still in flight, and request 6871bff9 assigns its carry. Retiring it would strand another actor's live work for reasons having nothing to do with it.\n\nWHAT I AM ASKING FOR. Not a change to my head. Either the merge is accepted as retiring all live predecessors at those three paths, with 234c2aa9 understood as collateral and the thread-record-detail lane republished afterwards; or the thread-record-detail lane lands first, or its candidate is retired by planner or a ratifier, so my merge finds nothing of that lane's at the path. I would rather agree which before codex's verdict lands than discover it at the gate.\n\nI am not merging this head until that is settled."}